=== PHASE P19 PARITY AUDIT (gif.c) ===
Source: Source/render/decoders/gif.lua (GIFDecoder) — ported faithfully.

Scope:
- Reject len<14; sig must be GIF87a/GIF89a.                             [G.short_input / G.bad_signature]
- LSD: screenW/H u16le, packed byte (GCT flag + size bits -> 1<<((p&7)+1));
  maxW/maxH `or` defaults 360/200 (<=0 → default in C).
- Global palette grays via rgbToGray; missing bytes -> entry 0.
- Block walk until first Image Descriptor: 0x3B/EOF -> nil;             [G.trailer_no_image]
  0x21 extensions skipped sub-block-wise; GCE 0xF9 transparency flag
  bit0 -> transparent index (byte may be absent == nil);
  unknown block bytes skipped by +1 exactly like the source.
- Image descriptor: left/top/w/h/packed; LOCAL palette overrides global;
  QUIRK preserved: imgTop is parsed but NEVER used — frame rows
  composite onto the canvas starting at row 0 (left offset only).       [D.offset]
- LZW sub-blocks concatenated into one bitstream; LSB-first codes read
  from overlapping byte triples; EOF mid-code == Lua nil.
- Dictionary: prefix/suffix tables with nil sentinels mirroring Lua's
  `prefix[code] >= 0` / `suffix[code] or code` walk; clear/end codes,
  widening when nextCode >= maxCode && codeSize < 12 after each add;
  speculative-entry path (code >= nextCode) pushes firstChar+oldCode;
  table capped at 4096.
- Streaming into ScaleAccum created with LOGICAL SCREEN dims; rows are
  frame rows composited over white at imgLeft; QUIRK: only imgH rows
  are ever added (output height == imgH when unscaled), NOT screenH.    [D.offset 30x8]
- flushRow pads the tail white; endStream flushes partial + remainder;
  runs spanning row boundaries survive via per-pixel emission loop.
- Interlace: pass order {0,8},{4,8},{2,4},{1,2} buffered per linear row,
  replayed after stream end (missing rows -> blankRow white).           [D.inter]
- Transparency: matching palette index renders as white (255).          [D.trans]
- Animated files: decode RETURNS after first frame completes.           [D.multi]
- tasks_yield_check() every 8 flushed rows (pixelCounter % 8).
- finish count==0 treated as failure (Lua would hand an empty grid to
  toImage); heap tables (~40KB) to stay inside Playdate stack limits.

Fixture tooling (tools/gen_gif_fixtures.py):
- Includes a GIF LZW ENCODER whose code-width schedule SHADOWS THE
  DECODER'S bookkeeping (one dictionary-add per data code starting with
  the second; widen right after that add). First attempt widened one
  emission early (classic "early change" desync) and was caught by an
  independent Python reference decoder before any C build.

Test-side bugs found during bring-up (decoder faithful throughout):
1) Encoder early-change desync (above) — fixed via shadow schedule.
2) Naive encoder blew up quadratically on periodic fixture data
   (dictionary strings grew unbounded) — match length capped at 64,
   which keeps streams valid.
3) D.offset expectation assumed output height == logical screen height;
   source only streams imgH rows -> fixed expectation to 30x8.
4) D.bench probes used point samples; box-filter averaging requires
   floor(mean(2x2)+0.5) goldens like the PNG fixtures.

Verification:
- Host harness [P10dbg]: 10 passed, 0 failed (TOTAL 132 across phases).
- ASAN build/run: clean exit, no reports (many alloc paths exercised).
- make gate: 0 errors / 0 warnings (stack-usage warning resolved by
  moving LZW tables to the heap).
- Simulator boot (this log): all phase gates green incl. [P19] 10/0.
- Benchmark: 600x400 GIF -> 300x200 in ~4 ms (sim dylib).
- Visual debug viewer: decoded bench GIF blitted alongside PNG/BMP.
